1
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:43,990
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:46,870
[Episode 11]

3
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:52,940
[Emergency]

4
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:58,920
It won't open again.

5
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:00,580
Let's change this lock later.

6
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:03,040
Do you have anything to eat?

7
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:05,120
Snacks, staple food, or anything filling.

8
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:05,790
What's wrong?

9
00:02:05,790 --> 00:02:06,560
There's nothing. What's up?

10
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:07,280
Zhengliang just

11
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,280
got a little dizzy when he stood up.

12
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,810
Seems like low blood sugar.

13
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:11,710
Then I'll go to the supermarket
to buy him something.

14
00:02:11,710 --> 00:02:12,120
Wouldn't that solve it?

15
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:12,430
Don't go.

16
00:02:12,430 --> 00:02:14,280
If you look for a bite to eat now,

17
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:15,840
-well, it'll be too late.
-Well, how about this?

18
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,310
You take that apple.

19
00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:18,430
This won't work either.

20
00:02:18,430 --> 00:02:19,240
Well, he can also drink this.

21
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,560
This drink.

22
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:21,030
If it really doesn't work,

23
00:02:21,030 --> 00:02:22,120
give him some glucose!

24
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:22,910
An IV drip!

25
00:02:22,910 --> 00:02:24,630
Okay, let him drink this first!

26
00:02:24,630 --> 00:02:25,750
Look at you.

27
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:27,030
You won't do any tests

28
00:02:27,030 --> 00:02:28,150
or blood work.

29
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:29,590
How am I supposed to treat you?

30
00:02:29,590 --> 00:02:31,000
If you insist on this,

31
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:31,680
I can only prescribe

32
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:33,240
a box of anti-diarrhea medicine for you.

33
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:34,840
But you can't leave after taking it.

34
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:35,710
You have to be monitored

35
00:02:35,710 --> 00:02:36,700
in the observation room for 2 hours.

36
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:40,200
[Emergency Room]

37
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:39,000
Honey.

38
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:41,590
You'd better take me

39
00:02:41,590 --> 00:02:42,870
to No. 1 Hospital.

40
00:02:43,310 --> 00:02:44,360
It's just a bad stomach.

41
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:45,680
You'll be fine once you get it all out.

42
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:46,680
If you travel that far,

43
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:47,590
can you even handle it?

44
00:02:47,590 --> 00:02:49,320
Besides, why spend that money?

45
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,520
Get lost!

46
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:54,280
I rummaged for a long time,
and there's only half a bottle left.

47
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,030
Drink it.

48
00:02:55,430 --> 00:02:56,680
What is this?

49
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:57,400
Whose leftovers?

50
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:58,470
You still mind drinking after me?

51
00:02:58,470 --> 00:02:59,430
If you're dizzy from hunger,

52
00:02:59,430 --> 00:03:01,430
I'll have to give you a glucose drip.

53
00:03:01,930 --> 00:03:02,710
Well,

54
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:05,430
she says she has acute gastroenteritis,

55
00:03:05,430 --> 00:03:06,750
but she refuses to do any tests.

56
00:03:06,750 --> 00:03:07,400
I can only prescribe

57
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:09,150
a box of anti-diarrhea medicine for her.

58
00:03:09,150 --> 00:03:09,960
After she takes it later,

59
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:10,280
you take her

60
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:11,560
to the observation room

61
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:13,000
for monitoring for 2 hours.

62
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:13,240
Okay.

63
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:15,040
Then let Huang take a look at her.

64
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,079
You go get the medicine.

65
00:03:17,079 --> 00:03:18,310
Let your wife go with him.

66
00:03:18,310 --> 00:03:19,560
Wait, after we get the medicine,

67
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:21,360
can't we just go home and take it?

68
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,190
Anyway, my advice is that

69
00:03:23,190 --> 00:03:25,000
you must stay for observation.

70
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:26,680
If you insist on leaving, you can,

71
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,710
but you have to sign.

72
00:03:27,710 --> 00:03:29,560
Honey, what are you doing?

73
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:31,300
Just listen to the doctor.

74
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:32,190
Okay, okay.

75
00:03:32,190 --> 00:03:32,870
Keep an eye out for me.

76
00:03:32,870 --> 00:03:33,590
I'll buy some food.

77
00:03:33,590 --> 00:03:34,720
Eat something warm.

78
00:03:34,910 --> 00:03:35,630
Look at you.

79
00:03:36,470 --> 00:03:37,710
Aren't you usually pretty tough?

80
00:03:37,710 --> 00:03:39,910
Come, the observation room is this way.

81
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:41,079
Let's go.

82
00:03:41,190 --> 00:03:42,590
"Yearning"

83
00:03:43,590 --> 00:03:45,560
by Li Bai from the Tang Dynasty.

84
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,030
Fresh autumn breeze, bright autumn moon.

85
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:52,420
Fallen leaves gather
and scatter around the trees;

86
00:03:52,630 --> 00:03:55,690
Cold-stricken crows soon fall asleep
and wake as soon.

87
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,960
I long for you.
When can I see your longing look?

88
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:03,400
How can I bear this lonely night,
this lonely nook?

89
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:40,860
[1314 Funeral Supplies]
[Xiaoximen Store]

90
00:04:40,950 --> 00:04:47,970
[Pandora] [Starry Night]

91
00:04:50,390 --> 00:04:54,630
♪ Everyone on earth knows I love you ♪

92
00:04:54,390 --> 00:04:56,830
[Fucheng Xiaoximen Hospital]

93
00:04:56,970 --> 00:04:59,050
[Cures fast, heals well.
Skilled, handsome, affordable.]

94
00:04:59,050 --> 00:05:03,180
[Liu Zhengliang, Star Chief Physician]
[Emergency Department]

95
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:03,000
You look pretty tough up close.

96
00:05:03,390 --> 00:05:04,310
Look at you.

97
00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:06,120
Your posture is quite stiff.

98
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,530
You always pull a long face.

99
00:05:12,870 --> 00:05:14,270
You probably forgot how to smile.

100
00:05:14,270 --> 00:05:15,560
Look at those teeth.

101
00:05:19,190 --> 00:05:21,190
Look at how things worked out for us.

102
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:29,250
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

103
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:22,190
Isn't this

104
00:05:22,190 --> 00:05:25,120
Dr. Liu, who gets more handsome
the more I look at him?

105
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:28,040
What, pretending you can't hear me?

106
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:28,830
Wait.

107
00:05:29,390 --> 00:05:30,310
Today,

108
00:05:30,310 --> 00:05:31,070
when you were at work,

109
00:05:31,070 --> 00:05:32,720
it wasn't convenient for you
to answer my question.

110
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:33,920
Can you answer it now?

111
00:05:35,510 --> 00:05:36,680
Please step aside.

112
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,750
My blood sugar is low.

113
00:05:37,750 --> 00:05:39,070
I need to find some food.

114
00:05:39,070 --> 00:05:40,670
Then you need to eat quickly.

115
00:05:41,159 --> 00:05:42,490
I'll help you find some.

116
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:45,000
Aren't they all closed?

117
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:47,940
It's pitch black
as far as the eye can see.

118
00:05:48,390 --> 00:05:49,850
But I have food at my place.

119
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:57,540
Swallowing saliva won't fill you up.

120
00:05:58,190 --> 00:05:58,920
How about this?

121
00:05:58,920 --> 00:05:59,480
Either

122
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,340
you come to my place for a hot meal,

123
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,560
or you just stand here staring blankly,

124
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,560
waiting to faint.

125
00:06:04,310 --> 00:06:05,710
Think about it yourself?

126
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:16,870
How does it taste?

127
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:22,560
A bit salty.

128
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:23,920
But having it occasionally

129
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:24,720
is fine.

130
00:06:25,750 --> 00:06:27,240
You're getting a free meal.

131
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:28,900
And you're still being picky?

132
00:06:29,510 --> 00:06:30,970
Why don't you just starve?

133
00:06:39,630 --> 00:06:40,360
Thank you.

134
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:45,880
What did you say?
I didn't hear you clearly.

135
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,970
What program are you watching?

136
00:06:52,270 --> 00:06:53,800
I usually like

137
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,920
poetry and songs, these kind of stuff.

138
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:56,830
Eat slowly.

139
00:06:58,240 --> 00:07:00,500
I like listening to people recite poetry

140
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,800
to cultivate myself.

141
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,750
Don't you dislike studying?

142
00:07:06,750 --> 00:07:08,240
Who dislikes studying?

143
00:07:08,830 --> 00:07:10,630
I love studying.

144
00:07:11,830 --> 00:07:12,510
Gosh.

145
00:07:12,510 --> 00:07:14,440
You even think I dislike studying.

146
00:07:14,630 --> 00:07:16,560
I just feel like throwing up
when I read books.

147
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:17,800
D-Did you

148
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:19,460
listen to me carefully today?

149
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:23,600
Understood.

150
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:25,510
So you

151
00:07:25,510 --> 00:07:26,920
don't like reading yourself,

152
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,920
but you like others reciting books.

153
00:07:31,270 --> 00:07:32,040
You're bad with words.

154
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,240
Just hurry up and eat.

155
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:40,600
Hello?

156
00:07:40,830 --> 00:07:43,310
Zhengliang, the patient is in shock.

157
00:07:44,070 --> 00:07:45,070
The one from just now,

158
00:07:45,070 --> 00:07:46,240
with acute gastroenteritis.

159
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:46,270
[Emergency Department–Yellow Zone]

160
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:46,600
Yes.

161
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:47,659
Come back quickly.

162
00:07:50,510 --> 00:07:51,970
What's up, Mr. Fake Smile?

163
00:07:52,310 --> 00:07:53,310
Running away after eating?

164
00:07:52,890 --> 00:07:54,890
[1314 Funeral Supplies]
[Xiaoximen Store]

165
00:08:27,870 --> 00:08:29,630
Mingming, what's the situation?

166
00:08:29,630 --> 00:08:30,650
Venous access has been established.

167
00:08:30,650 --> 00:08:31,770
Oxygen at 3 L/min.

168
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,390
BP 70 over 40.

169
00:08:33,390 --> 00:08:34,650
Oxygen saturation 90.

170
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:35,669
Heart rate 120.

171
00:08:37,850 --> 00:08:40,530
[Bed 2]

172
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,200
IV fluids for pressure support.

173
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:40,600
Normal saline 500 mL, wide open.

174
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:41,799
Normal saline 500 mL.

175
00:08:41,870 --> 00:08:42,840
Start another IV line.

176
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,600
Give 2 mg of norepinephrine.

177
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:45,510
Draw blood immediately.

178
00:08:45,510 --> 00:08:47,630
Get ABG and routine labs.

179
00:08:50,790 --> 00:08:52,030
BP dropped again.

180
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,340
Oxygen saturation 90.

181
00:08:53,550 --> 00:08:55,200
Titrate up the norepinephrine.

182
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,120
Get the BVM ready.

183
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:56,960
Ventilate.

184
00:08:57,670 --> 00:08:58,870
Call the anesthesiology department.

185
00:08:58,870 --> 00:09:01,070
Have them do endotracheal intubation.

186
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:11,200
Ventricular fibrillation.

187
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:16,550
Charge the defibrillator, quickly!

188
00:09:16,550 --> 00:09:17,750
360 joules.

189
00:09:17,750 --> 00:09:18,480
Ready.

190
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:32,020
Prepare for defibrillation.

191
00:09:43,790 --> 00:09:44,850
Give epinephrine,

192
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,750
1 mg IV push.

193
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:50,870
Continue.

194
00:09:58,160 --> 00:09:59,480
[Build the Line of Defence of Life]

195
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:07,300
[Fucheng Xiaoximen Hospital]

196
00:10:13,870 --> 00:10:18,420
[Outpatient Hall]

197
00:10:17,750 --> 00:10:19,410
Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang!

198
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,590
You killed my sis!

199
00:10:20,990 --> 00:10:22,990
Get out here and kowtow to apologize!

200
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:23,750
The one leading the trouble

201
00:10:23,750 --> 00:10:25,280
is the deceased's brother.

202
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:26,830
He's a contractor in Fucheng,

203
00:10:26,830 --> 00:10:28,040
and his business is quite big.

204
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:28,800
So this matter

205
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:29,950
won't be easily settled.

206
00:10:29,950 --> 00:10:31,560
They specifically
asked for Liu Zhengliang.

207
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:33,320
They insist he kowtows and kneels.

208
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:35,520
After all, from treatment to death,

209
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:36,320
it happened in less than an hour.

210
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:37,630
She didn't have any tests done.

211
00:10:37,630 --> 00:10:38,680
As for the cause of death,

212
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:40,320
Dr. Liu isn't clear about it either.

213
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:41,280
Also,

214
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:42,950
respect for the dead is paramount.

215
00:10:42,950 --> 00:10:43,990
In terms of public sympathy,

216
00:10:43,990 --> 00:10:45,520
he doesn't have the upper hand.

217
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:46,750
Tell Liu Zhengliang to hold back.

218
00:10:46,750 --> 00:10:47,230
Don't show up.

219
00:10:47,230 --> 00:10:48,400
I'll hurry to the police station.

220
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,560
Wait until I get back to do anything.

221
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:49,870
Okay, got it.

222
00:10:49,870 --> 00:10:52,000
Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

223
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:54,560
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

224
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:56,590
Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

225
00:10:56,590 --> 00:10:58,870
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

226
00:10:58,870 --> 00:11:00,920
Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

227
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:03,280
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

228
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:05,350
Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

229
00:11:05,350 --> 00:11:07,590
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

230
00:11:07,590 --> 00:11:09,720
Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

231
00:11:09,750 --> 00:11:12,470
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

232
00:11:12,470 --> 00:11:14,710
Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

233
00:11:14,830 --> 00:11:17,200
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

234
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:19,330
Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

235
00:11:19,350 --> 00:11:21,470
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

236
00:11:21,470 --> 00:11:23,600
Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang, get out!

237
00:11:30,750 --> 00:11:31,990
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang,
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang,

238
00:11:31,990 --> 00:11:33,750
-kowtow and confess!
-kowtow and confess!

239
00:11:33,750 --> 00:11:35,110
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang,
-Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang,

240
00:11:35,110 --> 00:11:36,470
-kowtow and confess!
-kowtow and confess!

241
00:11:36,470 --> 00:11:39,080
Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang,
kowtow and confess!

242
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:41,880
Quack Doctor Liu Zhengliang,
kowtow and confess!

243
00:11:41,950 --> 00:11:43,680
How long are you going to make a scene?

244
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:45,740
Finally, someone comes out to speak.

245
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:46,830
That guy named Liu Zhengliang,

246
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:47,400
where is he hiding?

247
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:48,530
Tell him to come out!

248
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:50,110
He's off today.

249
00:11:50,110 --> 00:11:51,460
If you have anything to say, tell us.

250
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:52,790
We'll pass it on for you.

251
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,630
Then call him over from home.

252
00:11:54,680 --> 00:11:56,740
I won't leave until he shows up today.

253
00:11:57,630 --> 00:11:58,630
Here's the thing.

254
00:11:58,750 --> 00:11:59,800
Ms. Shao Nan

255
00:11:59,870 --> 00:12:01,670
refused to do all kinds of tests.

256
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:03,080
We tried our best to persuade her,

257
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:04,400
and she finally stayed for observation.

258
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:06,110
As soon as she went into shock
in the observation room,

259
00:12:06,110 --> 00:12:07,080
we immediately took

260
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:08,280
emergency measures.

261
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,680
From registration to the patient's death,

262
00:12:09,680 --> 00:12:10,990
it happened in less than an hour.

263
00:12:10,990 --> 00:12:11,710
Our emergency department

264
00:12:11,710 --> 00:12:13,040
has done everything we could.

265
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:13,870
We wanted her to live

266
00:12:13,870 --> 00:12:15,130
more than anyone else.

267
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:16,470
How can you be so sure

268
00:12:16,470 --> 00:12:16,830
that all of this

269
00:12:16,830 --> 00:12:18,110
is the doctor's fault?

270
00:12:18,110 --> 00:12:19,590
A perfectly fine person was sent here,

271
00:12:19,590 --> 00:12:20,320
and now she's gone!

272
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:22,320
Who else should I blame if not the doctor?

273
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:23,980
I can understand how you feel,

